.TH SKMP 1 "May 2024" "skmp" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
skmp \- Skill marketplace for AI agent skills
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B skmp
[COMMAND] [FLAGS]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B skmp
is a TUI application and CLI tool to discover, install, and manage skills for AI coding agents (such as pi, claude-code, opencode, codex, and cursor).

Running
.B skmp
without any arguments launches the interactive terminal user interface (TUI).
.SH INTERACTIVE TUI
Inside the TUI, you can navigate and manage skills using the following keybindings:
.TP
.B j, \(da
Move cursor down
.TP
.B k, \(ua
Move cursor up
.TP
.B 1, 2, 3, 4
Switch tabs (Skills, Bundles, My Skills, My Bundles)
.TP
.B Tab
Switch focus between the list pane and the detail pane
.TP
.B /
Focus the search input (press \fBEsc\fR or \fBEnter\fR to leave)
.TP
.B i
Install the currently selected skill or bundle
.TP
.B x
Remove the currently selected skill or bundle
.TP
.B ?
Toggle the help overlay
.TP
.B q, Ctrl+C
Quit the application

.SH COMMANDS
.TP
.B add <skill> [skill...]
Install one or more skills by name.
.br
\fB\-b, \-\-bundle\fR \fI<bundle>\fR: Install all skills from a specified bundle.
.TP
.B list
List all currently installed skills.
.TP
.B remove <skill> [skill...]
Uninstall one or more skills.
.TP
.B sync
Sync installed skills from the internal store to all detected agent harnesses.
.TP
.B update
Update the local skill registry cache from GitHub.
.TP
.B uninstall
Remove all skmp data, symlinks, and configuration from your system.
.br
\fB\-\-force\fR: Skip the interactive confirmation prompt.
.TP
.B version
Print the current skmp version.

.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.skmp/skills
Internal store where skmp downloads and manages skills.
.TP
.I ~/.agents/skills
Standard directory for pi and claude-code skills (skmp creates symlinks here).
.TP
.I ~/.config/opencode/opencode.jsonc
OpenCode configuration file (skmp safely registers its store path here).
.TP
.I ~/.cursor/mcp.json
Cursor configuration used to detect if Cursor is installed.
.TP
.I ~/.codex/skills
Codex skills directory.

